{# Design's market page — `design_handoff_market_reports/Report Page.dc.html`.

   ONE PAGE, DISPATCHED ON KIND, which is their architecture and ours:
   `market.jinja2` already dispatched on `LAYOUT_MAP`, and their README says so
   ("`market.jinja2` already dispatches on layout; add the `listings` density
   switch and the shared band/table partials"). This is the shared band plus the
   table body; only the kinds in `market_builder.V2_KINDS` render it.

   WHAT IS NOT HERE, AND WHY. No running head and no footer: those are PDFShift's
   repeating `header` and `footer`, rendered by `_base/page_header.jinja2` and
   `_base/page_footer.jinja2` at `start_at = 1`, and the 0.44in / 0.89in they
   reserve is what gives this body its 9.67in. Design's mapping confirms the
   placement and that our reservation already fits their 40px bar "with 2px to
   spare — keep 0.44in, don't resize the head."

   The masthead band below is BODY CONTENT, page 1 only, never a header — also
   their mapping. It is why page 1 holds fewer rows than a continuation page, and
   why their 3x2 gallery grid on page 1 is the band's cost rather than a grid
   decision.

   NO AI NARRATIVE. Design removes it from the table kinds so page-1 capacity is
   one state per kind; `market_builder` suppresses it for `V2_KINDS` before the
   generate call. Measured: 11 rows with it, 15 without. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ v2_band.title }}{% if header.city %} — {{ header.city }}{% endif %}</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    /* The brand colour AS THE FILL. Not the darkened two-stop band: every text
       colour on it is derived from it, so the text adapts rather than the fill
       being bent to fit text hardcoded to white (D-112). */
    --primary: {{ primary_color }};
    --on-primary: {{ on_primary }};
    --display-ink: {{ display_ink }};
    --primary-ink: {{ primary_ink }};
    --accent: {{ accent_color }};
    /* Design's `accent_ink`, which is our `accent_on_light` — one token, two
       vocabularies, see docs/MARKET_TOKEN_MAPPING_2026-10-07.md. Guaranteed
       >=4.5 on white AND on the tint since D-177. */
    --accent-ink: {{ accent_on_light }};
    --tint: {{ tint }};
    --on-primary-rule: {{ on_primary_rule }};

    /* Design's neutrals, with their measured contrast on white. */
    --ink: #14161A;        /* 18.1:1 */
    --body: #2A2D33;       /* 13.8:1 */
    --muted: {{ v2_muted }};       /* 6.05:1 — the lightest text on the surface */
    --rule: #ECECE8;
    --rule-soft: #E4E4E0;

    --font: 'Geist', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    --mono: 'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
  }

  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  body {
    font-family: var(--font);
    color: var(--body);
    background: #ffffff;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  /* ── The page-1 band (shared across kinds) ──────────────────────────────
     FIXED HEIGHT BY CONSTRUCTION, which is Design's requirement: "band height
     is therefore fixed: nothing in it grows with data." The label sits in a
     50px box and steps its type size down by character count rather than
     wrapping — `market_builder._v2_label_size`, their ladder. */
  .band {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: var(--on-primary);
    padding: 30px 52px 26px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 30px;
  }
  .band-top {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 24px;
  }
  .band-title {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--on-primary);
  }
  .band-logo { max-height: 44px; max-width: 200px; width: auto; object-fit: contain; }
  .band-brand { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--on-primary); }

  .band-lead { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 24px; }
  .band-lead-left { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 18px; min-width: 0; }
  .band-big {
    font-size: 88px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 0.88;
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    white-space: nowrap;
    color: var(--display-ink);
  }
  /* THE FIXED 50px BOX. The type steps, the box does not. */
  .band-label-box {
    height: 50px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-end;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding-bottom: 3px;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  /* `on_primary`, NOT `display_ink`, AND THE PIXEL GATE IS WHY.
     The ladder's largest step is 22px at weight 600 — which is NOT large text
     by either of WCAG 1.4.3's definitions (>=24px, or >=18.66px at >=700), so
     it needs 4.5 and `display_ink`'s threshold is 3.0. Design specifies white
     here; measured, that is 3.74:1 on #0d9488. Every step of the ladder (22,
     18, 15, 13) is below 24px, so the token is wrong for this element at every
     size it can take.
     This is `.cover-city` on the property surface, one day later, on a
     different surface and from the same package. The 88px number and the 26px
     stat values ARE large text and keep `display_ink`. */
  .band-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--on-primary);
    white-space: pre-line;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
  }
  .band-lead-right { text-align: right; flex-shrink: 0; }
  /* `primary_ink`, NOT `primary`. Design specifies "white pill, `primary`
     text" — the RAW BRAND COLOUR on white, at 13px/600, which is not large
     text. Measured: 3.74:1 on teal, 2.15 on amber, 1.98 on lime. `primary_ink`
     is the brand darkened until it clears AA on white and on the tint
     (D-170, D-177), which is the token that exists for brand-coloured text on
     a light surface. The FILL stays white and the brand stays recognisable. */
  .band-pill {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: var(--primary-ink);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 4px 10px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .band-pill-sub { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--on-primary); margin-top: 6px; }

  .band-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat({{ v2_band.cells | length }}, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-top: 1px solid var(--on-primary-rule);
    padding-top: 16px;
  }
  .band-stat { padding-right: 16px; }
  .band-stat + .band-stat { border-left: 1px solid var(--on-primary-rule); padding-left: 16px; }
  .band-stat-value {
    font-size: 26px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--display-ink);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .band-stat-label { font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--on-primary); margin-top: 3px; }

  /* ── The table ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Design's grid: `1fr 64 72 108 72 44`. A GRID, not a <table>, because the
     column widths are the spec and a table would negotiate them. */
  .table { padding: 22px 52px 0; }
  /* ROW HEIGHT IS DERIVED FROM DESIGN'S ROW COUNT, not chosen.
     They state 13 rows on page 1 and 26 on a continuation page and do not state
     a height. A market page's body is 9.67in = 928px, so 26 rows means
     928 / 26 = 35.7px per row INCLUDING its rule. The first version used
     `padding: 7px 0` with default line-heights, measured 19 rows per
     continuation page, and would have cost two pages per report against their
     spec. These values are what 26 requires:
         address 13px x 1.15 = 15.0   +   hood 11.5px x 1.15 = 13.2
       + padding 2 x 3px     =  6.0   +   rule 1px
       = 35.2px  ->  26 rows = 915px of 928  (measured: 13 and 26)
     MEASURED, AND DESIGN'S TWO NUMBERS DO NOT AGREE WITH EACH OTHER.
     26 continuation rows requires a row of at most (928 - 22) / 26 = 34.8px.
     13 page-1 rows at that height requires a page-1 chrome of 441-476px
     (band + table padding + header row). Their band spec — padding 30/26,
     gap 30, a 44px logo slot, an 88px number at line-height 0.88, a stats row
     — computes to about 295px, and ours measures 265. So no single row height
     satisfies both of their numbers against their own band: hitting 26 puts
     page 1 at 17, and hitting 13 would put the continuation page at 19 and
     cost two pages per report.

     Resolved by hitting the CONTINUATION number, because that is the one that
     drives page count on a 200-row report, and reporting the page-1 overshoot
     with the arithmetic. 17 on page 1 is more rows than they specified, which
     costs the customer nothing — it is fewer pages, not more. */
  .trow {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 64px 72px 108px 72px 44px;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0 12px;
    padding: 2px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .thead {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
    padding-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .tnum { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .taddr { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.05; color: var(--ink);
           overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
  .thood { font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.05; color: var(--muted); }
  .tcell { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.15; color: var(--body); }
  /* Design: ">100% in `accent_ink` 600, else `#5E636B` 400". The boolean is
     resolved in Python — a template cannot ask whether a ratio is above a
     threshold without reimplementing the threshold. */
  .tvs-over { color: var(--accent-ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .tvs-under { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 400; }

  .tshowing {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 9.5px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding: 12px 52px 0;
  }

  /* Rows must not split across a page break; the paginator decides where the
     break goes and the fit gate measures what that yields. */
  .trow { break-inside: avoid; page-break-inside: avoid; }

  @media print {
    body { background: #ffffff; }
    .band { break-inside: avoid; page-break-inside: avoid; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<section class="band">
  <div class="band-top">
    <div class="band-title">{{ v2_band.title }}</div>
    {% if agent.logo_url %}
    <img class="band-logo" src="{{ agent.logo_url }}" alt="">
    {% elif agent.brand_name %}
    <div class="band-brand">{{ agent.brand_name }}</div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="band-lead">
    <div class="band-lead-left">
      <div class="band-big">{{ v2_band.big }}</div>
      <div class="band-label-box">
        <span class="band-label" style="font-size: {{ v2_band.label_px }}px">{{ v2_band.label }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% if v2_band.pill %}
    <div class="band-lead-right">
      <span class="band-pill">{{ v2_band.pill }}</span>
      {% if v2_band.pill_sub %}<div class="band-pill-sub">{{ v2_band.pill_sub }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="band-stats">
    {% for cell in v2_band.cells %}
    <div class="band-stat">
      <div class="band-stat-value">{{ cell.value }}</div>
      <div class="band-stat-label">{{ cell.label }}</div>
    </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="table">
  <div class="trow thead">
    <div>Address</div>
    <div class="tnum">Bd/Ba</div>
    <div class="tnum">Sq ft</div>
    <div class="tnum">Sold for</div>
    <div class="tnum">vs. list</div>
    <div class="tnum">Days</div>
  </div>
  {% for row in v2_table.rows %}
  <div class="trow">
    <div>
      <div class="taddr">{{ row.address }}</div>
      {% if row.hood %}<div class="thood">{{ row.hood }}</div>{% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="tcell tnum">{{ row.beds_baths }}</div>
    <div class="tcell tnum">{{ row.sqft }}</div>
    <div class="tcell tnum">{{ row.price }}</div>
    <div class="tnum {{ 'tvs-over' if row.vs_over else 'tvs-under' }}">{{ row.vs_list }}</div>
    <div class="tcell tnum">{{ row.days }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

{# "Showing a–b of N". The page number is NOT here: this document does not know
   how the paginator will break it, and a page number written by the body would
   be wrong on every page but one. PDFShift's footer carries `Page x of P`. #}
<div class="tshowing">
  {% if v2_table.showing < v2_table.total %}
  Showing {{ v2_table.showing }} of {{ v2_table.total }}
  {% else %}
  {{ v2_table.total }} {{ 'sale' if v2_table.total == 1 else 'sales' }}
  {% endif %}
</div>

</body>
</html>
